      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 94, lettuce kept as one entry for all types (cos, butterhead, crisphead, loose-leaf); a cut-and-come-again salad mix is not this entry. A short-cycle annual: sow, pick, clear (head types about three months, loose leaf about a month to first pick, RHS). Sources: NC State, Missouri BG (taxon 263870; 271393 also opened, a cultivar page, not cited), RHS grow-your-own page. No ASPCA entry for lettuce, so pets read 'not assessed'. People: NC State lists contact dermatitis from the sap (low severity, lactucin and lactucopicrin); graded 1 for skin by the agent. Conflict: none on care; NC State says full sun to partial shade, RHS a sunny spot with light shade in midsummer; 'part' chosen as the gentler reading. Size 30 by 30 cm is the agent's mapping of 6 to 12 in. No hardiness (annual). Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
